    devanagari: 'ॐ विशुद्धज्ञानदेहाय त्रिवेदीदिव्यचक्षुषे।\nश्रेयःप्राप्तिनिमित्ताय नमः सोमार्धधारिणे॥१॥\nसर्वमेतद्विजानीयान्मन्त्राणामपि कीलकम्।\nसोऽपि क्षेममवाप्नोति सततं जप्यतत्परः॥२॥\nसिद्ध्यन्त्युच्चाटनादीनि कर्माणि सकलान्यपि।\nएतेन स्तुवतां देवीं स्तोत्रवृन्देन भक्तितः॥३॥\nन मन्त्रो नौषधं तत्र न किञ्चिदपि विद्यते।\nविना जप्येन सिद्ध्येत्तु सर्वमुच्चाटनादिकम्॥४॥\nसमग्राण्यपि सेत्स्यन्ति लोकशङ्कामिमां हरः।\nकृत्वा निमन्त्रयामास सर्वमेवमिदं शुभम्॥५॥\nस्तोत्रं वै चण्डिकायास्तु तच्च गुह्यं चकार सः।\nसमाप्नोति स पुण्येन तां यथावन्निमन्त्रणाम्॥६॥',
    iast: 'oṃ viśuddhajñānadehāya trivedīdivyacakṣuṣe |\nśreyaḥprāptinimittāya namaḥ somārdhadhāriṇe ||1||\nsarvametadvijānīyānmantrāṇāmapi kīlakam |\nso\'pi kṣemamavāpnoti satataṃ jāpyatatparaḥ ||2||\nsiddhyantyuccāṭanādīni karmāṇi sakalānyapi |\netena stuvatāṃ devīṃ stotravṛndena bhaktitaḥ ||3||\nna mantro nauṣadhaṃ tatra na kiñcidapi vidyate |\nvinā jāpyena siddhyettu sarvamuccāṭanādikam ||4||\nsamagrāṇyapi setsyanti lokaśaṅkāmimāṃ haraḥ |\nkṛtvā nimantrayāmāsa sarvamevamidaṃ śubham ||5||\nstotraṃ vai caṇḍikāyāstu tacca guhyaṃ cakāra saḥ |\nsamāpnoti sa puṇyena tāṃ yathāvannimantraṇām ||6||',
    conceptIds: ['sadhana-samara', 'mahamaya'],
    translation: 'Om. Salutation to Him of pure-knowledge body, three-Veda divine eyes, giver of welfare, half-moon bearer (Śiva-Śakti). Know all this as the Pin (kīlaka) of mantras; devotees attain peace. By praising Devī with this host of hymns with devotion, all acts including eradication (uccāṭana) succeed. Doubting how violent mantras grant good, Hara (Śiva) pinned and hid this Caṇḍikā-hymn; rightly invoked it yields merit.',
    commentary: `**Sādhana-Samara Commentary (Hindi: kīlaka = śāpa + adhikāra):**
1. **Vishuddha-jnana-deha**: The Conscious Form (cit-rūpa) of Devi is pinned to every Saptaśatī mantra. Shiva-Shakti share half-moon (somārdha): pure knowledge + three-Veda vision. Meditation is not on war-killing but on that Conscious Form.
2. **Why a pin?** Saptaśatī looks violent; people doubt how killing grants śubha. Shiva pinned (kīlita) the text and hid (guhya) its true object so mechanical recitation without devotion gives little. Uccāṭana here is inner — eradication of foes (lust-anger) to the root, not black magic. No mantra, no medicine works without this japa-attitude.
3. **For beginners**: First learn the key (adhikāra): surrender + meditation on Conscious Mother. Then every mantra opens. This is true śāpoddhāra.`,
    keyPoints: [
      '**Pinned Conscious Form**: Every violent verse hides meditation on pure-knowledge Mother.',
      '**Uccāṭana = Inner Eradication**: Rooting out inner foes, not harming others.',
      '**Key First**: Know the pin, then recite; otherwise doubt blocks fruit.'
    ]
