    devanagari: 'तामेवं स्तूयमाना तु तदा देवी तमोमयी।\nविष्णोर्नेत्रानननासाबाहुहृदयेभ्यस्तथोरसः॥८५॥\nनिर्गम्य दर्शयामास ब्रह्मणे धातृयोनये।\nतामुत्तीर्णां तदा देवीं भगवान् परमेश्वरः॥८७॥\nउत्तस्थौ च जगन्नाथस्तत्याज च स योगनिद्राम्।\nस च तौ वासुदेवेन युयुधे पञ्चवर्षसहस्रकम्॥९०॥\nतावप्यतिबलोन्मत्तौ महामायाविमोहितौ।\nउक्तवन्तौ वरोऽस्मत्तो व्रियतामिति केशवम्॥९२॥\nताभ्यां विहस्य भगवान् उवाच मधुसूदनः।\nवध्यौ मम भवेतां वै किमन्येन वरेण वः॥९४॥\nतावेवमुक्त्वा तौ दैत्यौ निरीक्ष्य च समन्ततः।\nसलिलाप्लुतभुवनं प्राहतुः कमलेक्षणम्॥९६॥\nआवां जहि न यत्रोर्वी सलिलेन परिप्लुता।\nतथेत्युक्त्वा भगवता शङ्खचक्रगदाभृता॥९८॥\nकृत्वा चक्रेण वै छिन्ने जघने शिरसी तयोः।\nएवमेषा समुत्पन्ना ब्रह्मणा संस्तुता निशा॥१००॥',
    iast: 'tāmevaṃ stūyamānā tu tadā devī tamomayī |\nviṣṇornetrānanāsābāhuhṛdayebhyastathorasaḥ ||85||\nnirgamya darśayāmāsa brahmaṇe dhātṛyonaye |\ntāmuttīrṇāṃ tadā devīṃ bhagavān parameśvaraḥ ||87||\nuttasthau ca jagannāthastatyāja ca sa yoganidrām |\nsa ca tau vāsudevena yuyudhe pañcavarṣasahasrakam ||90||\ntāvapyatibalōnmattau mahāmāyāvimohitau |\nuktavantau varo\'smatto vriyatāmiti keśavam ||92||\ntābhyāṃ vihasya bhagavān uvāca madhusūdanaḥ |\nvadhyau mama bhavetāṃ vai kimanyena vareṇa vaḥ ||94||\ntāvevamuktvā tau daityau nirīkṣya ca samantataḥ |\nsalilāplutabhuvanaṃ prāhatuḥ kamalekṣaṇam ||96||\nāvāṃ jahi na yatrōrvī salilena pariplutā |\ntathetyuktvā bhagavatā śaṅkhacakragadābhṛtā ||98||\nkṛtvā cakreṇa vai chinne jaghane śirasī tayoḥ |\nevameṣā samutpannā brahmaṇā saṃstutā niśā ||100||',
    conceptIds: ['madhu-kaitabha', 'mahamaya', 'sadhana-samara'],
    translation: 'Thus praised, dark Night withdrew from Viṣṇu’s eyes-mouth-nostrils-arms-heart-breast and showed Herself to Brahmā. Freed, the Lord rose, left Yoga-sleep, fought the demons 5000 years arm-to-arm. Drunk with power, deluded by Mahāmāyā, they told Viṣṇu “ask a boon!” Smiling He said “be slain by Me — what other boon?” Seeing world flooded, they said “slay where earth is not flooded.” “So be it,” He placed them on His thighs and beheaded them with discus. Thus was Night born of Brahmā’s praise.',
    commentary: `**Sādhana-Samara Commentary:**
1. **Withdrawal through senses**: Yoganidrā exits exactly where She entered — eyes (seeing), mouth-nose (tasting-breathing), arms-heart-breast (grasping-feeling). Sādhanā reverses this: withdraw Mother-power from outer sensing to awaken Will.
2. **5000-year arm-fight**: No outer weapon works on deep inertia-obstinacy; only prolonged self-effort (bāhu-yuddha) matures. Deluded by Mahāmāyā they offer a boon to their foe — ego blinded offers its neck. Viṣṇu’s smile (vihasya) = compassion, not mockery.
3. **Thighs (jaghana) trick**: “Not flooded” = firm ground beyond flux. Thighs = grounded tapas, ethical seat. Placing demons on thighs = bringing tamas-rajas onto firm practice-ground, then discus (sudden viveka-chakra) severs heads (ego-centres). Brahma-granthi pierced; tamas lifts; higher awareness stirs. Here ends Prathama Carita (Mahākālī).`,
