    devanagari: 'नमो देव्यै महादेव्यै शिवायै सततं नमः ।\nनमः प्रकृत्यै भद्रायै नियताः प्रणताः स्म ताम् ॥७॥\nरौद्रायै नमो नित्यायै गौर्यै धात्र्यै नमो नमः ।\nज्योत्स्नायै चेन्दुरूपिण्यै सुखायै सततं नमः ॥८॥\nकल्याण्यै प्रणतावृद्ध्यै सिद्ध्यै कूर्म्यै नमो नमः ।\nनैऋत्यै भूभृतां लक्ष्म्यै शर्वाण्यै ते नमो नमः ॥९॥\nदुर्गायै दुर्गपारायै सारायै सर्वकारिण्यै ।\nख्यात्यै तथैव कृष्णायै धूम्रायै सततं नमः ॥१०॥\nअतिसौम्यातिरौद्रायै नतास्तस्यै नमो नमः ।\nनमो जगत्प्रतिष्ठायै देव्यै कृत्यै नमो नमः ॥११॥\nया देवी सर्वभूतेषु विष्णुमायेति शब्दिता ।\nनमस्तस्यै नमस्तस्यै नमस्तस्यै नमो नमः ॥१२॥\nया देवी सर्वभूतेषु चेतनेत्यभिधीयते ।\nनमस्तस्यै नमस्तस्यै नमस्तस्यै नमो नमः ॥१३॥',
    iast: 'namo devyai mahādevyai śivāyai satataṃ namaḥ |\nnamaḥ prakṛtyai bhadrāyai niyatāḥ praṇatāḥ sma tām ||7||\nraudrāyai namo nityāyai gauryai dhātryai namo namaḥ |\njyotsnāyai cendurūpiṇyai sukhāyai satataṃ namaḥ ||8||\nkalyāṇyai praṇatāvṛddhyai siddhyai kūrmyai namo namaḥ |\nnaiṛtyai bhūbhṛtāṃ lakṣmyai śarvāṇyai te namo namaḥ ||9||\ndurgāyai durgapārāyai sārāyai sarvakāriṇyai |\nkhyātyai tathaiva kṛṣṇāyai dhūmrāyai satataṃ namaḥ ||10||\natisaumyātiraudrāyai natāstasyai namo namaḥ |\nnamo jagatpratiṣṭhāyai devyai kṛtyai namo namaḥ ||11||\nyā devī sarvabhūteṣu viṣṇumāyeti śabditā |\nnamastasyai namastasyai namastasyai namo namaḥ ||12||\nyā devī sarvabhūteṣu cetanetyabhidhīyate |\nnamastasyai namastasyai namastasyai namo namaḥ ||13||',
    conceptIds: ['cit-shakti', 'aparajita-stuti', 'sadhana-samara'],
    translation: '“Salutation to Devī, to Mahādevī, to Śivā ever; salutation to Prakṛti, to Bhadrā; disciplined, we bow to Her. To Raudrā, to Nityā, to Gaurī, to Dhātrī, salutation again; to Jyotsnā, to Indurūpiṇī, to Sukhā, salutation ever. To Kalyāṇī, to Her who increases the bowed, to Siddhi, to Kūrmī, salutation again; to Nairṛtī, to Lakṣmī of kings, to Śarvāṇī — to Thee, salutation. To Durgā, to Durgapārā, to Sārā, to Sarvakāriṇī; to Khyāti, and to Kṛṣṇā, to Dhūmrā, salutation ever. To the Exceeding-Gentle and Exceeding-Fierce we bow, salutation; salutation to Her who grounds the world, to Devī, to Kṛti. To the Goddess who in all beings is called Viṣṇu-māyā — salutation to Her, salutation to Her, salutation to Her, salutation again and again! To the Goddess who in all beings is called Awareness (cetanā) — salutation to Her, salutation to Her, salutation to Her, salutation again and again!”',
    commentary: `**Sādhana-Samara Commentary (Aparājitā opens; naming every face):**
1. **Why so many names?** Each name is one function of single Cit-Śakti turned Mother-ward (matṛ-mukhī): Raudrā (fierce against foes), Nityā (time-free), Gaurī (radiant), Dhātrī (nurse), Jyotsnā (moonlight-calm), Sukhā (ease), Kalyāṇī (welfare), Siddhi (accomplishment), Kūrmī (the Tortoise-power that bears worlds, Guptavatī), Nairṛtī (the southwest guardian assimilated), Śarvāṇī (Śiva’s own), Durgā-Durgapārā (fort and fort-crosser), Kṛṣṇā-Dhūmrā (dark and smoky veils), Atisaumyā-Atiraudrā (both extremes at once). For beginners: pick the name matching your lack and repeat it — every name is a door.
2. **Viṣṇu-māyā and cetanā first**: the “yā devī” series opens with Her as Viṣṇu’s deluding power and as bare Awareness — delusion and consciousness are the same Goddess seen outward and inward. Nāgojī: cetanā is nirvikalpā cit-śakti (choiceless awareness); buddhi (next, dm-5-14/dm-5-15) is its determinate wave. Worship Awareness before intellect.
3. **Triple bow (namastasyai ×3)**: body, mind and Self surrendered — or the three guṇas laid at Her feet. Jagaccandrikā counts three mantras per verse (word, half, whole): recite slowly, letting each naming land. The series continues (dm-5-15 onward) through sleep, hunger, shadow, power, thirst, patience — no function left unbowed.`,
    keyPoints: [
      '**Every Name a Door**: Each function of one Śakti — pick the name matching your lack.',
      '**Delusion = Awareness**: Viṣṇu-māyā outward, cetanā inward — one Goddess both ways.',
      '**Triple Bow**: Body, mind, Self — or three guṇas — laid at Her feet.'
    ]
