    devanagari: 'या देवी सर्वभूतेषु स्मृतिरूपेण संस्थिता ।\nनमस्तस्यै नमस्तस्यै नमस्तस्यै नमो नमः ॥२८॥\nया देवी सर्वभूतेषु दयारूपेण संस्थिता ।\nनमस्तस्यै नमस्तस्यै नमस्तस्यै नमो नमः ॥२९॥\nया देवी सर्वभूतेषु तुष्टिरूपेण संस्थिता ।\nनमस्तस्यै नमस्तस्यै नमस्तस्यै नमो नमः ॥३०॥\nया देवी सर्वभूतेषु मातृरूपेण संस्थिता ।\nनमस्तस्यै नमस्तस्यै नमस्तस्यै नमो नमः ॥३१॥\nया देवी सर्वभूतेषु भ्रान्तिरूपेण संस्थिता ।\nनमस्तस्यै नमस्तस्यै नमस्तस्यै नमो नमः ॥३२॥\nइन्द्रियाणामधिष्ठात्री भूतानामखिलेषु या ।\nभूतेषु सततं तस्यै व्याप्त्यै देव्यै नमो नमः ॥३३॥\nचितिरूपेण या कृत्स्नमेतद्व्याप्य स्थिता जगत् ।\nनमस्तस्यै नमस्तस्यै नमस्तस्यै नमो नमः ॥३४॥\nस्तुता सुरैः पूर्वमभीष्टसंश्रयात्तथा सुरेन्द्रेण दिनेषु सेविता ।\nकरोतु सा नः शुभहेतुरीश्वरी शुभानि भद्राण्यभिहन्तु चापदः ॥३५॥\nया साम्प्रतं चोद्धतदैत्यतापितैरस्माभिरीशा च सुरैर्नमस्यते ।\nया च स्मृता तत्क्षणमेव हन्ति नः सर्वापदो भक्तिविनम्रमूर्तिभिः ॥३६॥',
    iast: 'yā devī sarvabhūteṣu smṛtirūpeṇa saṃsthitā |\nnamastasyai namastasyai namastasyai namo namaḥ ||28||\nyā devī sarvabhūteṣu dayārūpeṇa saṃsthitā |\nnamastasyai namastasyai namastasyai namo namaḥ ||29||\nyā devī sarvabhūteṣu tuṣṭirūpeṇa saṃsthitā |\nnamastasyai namastasyai namastasyai namo namaḥ ||30||\nyā devī sarvabhūteṣu mātṛrūpeṇa saṃsthitā |\nnamastasyai namastasyai namastasyai namo namaḥ ||31||\nyā devī sarvabhūteṣu bhrāntirūpeṇa saṃsthitā |\nnamastasyai namastasyai namastasyai namo namaḥ ||32||\nindriyāṇāmadhiṣṭhātrī bhūtānāmakhileṣu yā |\nbhūteṣu satataṃ tasyai vyāptyai devyai namo namaḥ ||33||\ncitirūpeṇa yā kṛtsnametadvyāpya sthitā jagat |\nnamastasyai namastasyai namastasyai namo namaḥ ||34||\nstutā suraiḥ pūrvamabhīṣṭasaṃśrayāttathā surendreṇa dineṣu sevitā |\nkarotu sā naḥ śubhaheturīśvarī śubhāni bhadrāṇyabhihantu cāpadaḥ ||35||\nyā sāmprataṃ coddhatadaityatāpitairasmābhirīśā ca surairnamasyate |\nyā ca smṛtā tatkṣaṇameva hanti naḥ sarvāpado bhaktivinamramūrtibhiḥ ||36||',
    conceptIds: ['cit-shakti', 'aparajita-stuti', 'sadhana-samara'],
    translation: '“To the Goddess who abides in all beings as Memory (smṛti)… Compassion (dayā)… Contentment (tuṣṭi)… Motherhood (mātṛ)… Delusion itself (bhrānti) — salutation to Her ×3, again and again! To Her who presides over the senses, who is in all beings — to Her, to Pervasion, to Devī, salutation again! To Her who, as Consciousness (citi), stands pervading all this world — salutation ×3, again! Praised of yore by gods seeking refuge and served daily by Indra, may She, the blessed Īśvarī, cause of weal, grant us good, destroy calamity. And who NOW is worshipped by us gods, tormented by insolent demons — who, remembered, instantly slays our perils for those bowed in devotion.”',
    commentary: `**Sādhana-Samara Commentary (delusion itself bowed to; praise becomes contract):**
1. **Bhrānti — the boldest bow**: memory, compassion, contentment, motherhood — then DELUSION (bhrānti)! Even error is Her veiled face (cf. dm-1-54: She forcibly deludes the wise). Do not hate your confusions; bow to the power in them and they release their grip. Mātṛ just before bhrānti is deliberate: the same Mother mothers and mazes.
2. **Pervasion and citi close the series**: adhiṣṭhātrī (presiding over senses), vyāpti (pervasion itself), citi (consciousness spanning all) — from many functions to Functioning itself. Nāgojī: citi is nirvikalpā (choiceless); buddhi (ed14) was its determinate wave. The series climbs: parts → whole → awareness.
3. **“NOW” (sāmpratam)**: the stuti turns from timeless praise to present contract — worshipped NOW by US, tormented NOW; remembered, She kills perils INSTANTLY (tatkṣaṇam). Stuti is not literature; it is a standing offer. Claim it: remember, and watch peril thin. Next: Pārvatī comes to bathe (dm-5-37) — praise bears fruit as embodiment.`,
