    section: 'Uttama Carita (Rudra-Granthi Bheda / Śumbha-Niśumbha Vadha)',
    devanagari: 'तदागच्छतु शुम्भोऽत्र निशुम्भो वा महासुरः ।\nमां जित्वा किं चिरेणात्र पाणिं गृह्णातु मे लघु ॥७०॥\nदूत उवाच ।\nअवलिप्तासि मैवं त्वं देवि ब्रूहि ममाग्रतः ।\nत्रैलोक्ये कः पुमस्तिष्ठेदग्रे शुम्भनिशुम्भयोः ॥७१॥\nअन्येषामपि दैत्यानां सर्वे देवा न वै युधि ।\nतिष्ठन्ति सम्मुखे देवि किं पुनः स्त्री त्वमेकिका ॥७२॥\nइन्द्राद्याः सकला देवास्तस्थुर्येषां न संयुगे ।\nशुम्भादीनां कथं तेषां स्त्री प्रयास्यसि सम्मुखम् ॥७३॥\nसा त्वं गच्छ मयैवोक्ता पार्श्व शुम्भनिशुम्भयोः ।\nकेशाकर्षणनिर्धूतगौरवा मा गमिष्यसि ॥७४॥\nएवमेतद्बली शुम्भो निशुम्भश्चातिवीर्यवान् ।\nकिं करोमि प्रतिज्ञा मे यदनालोचिता पुरा ॥७५॥\nस त्वं गच्छ मयैवोक्तं यदेतत्सर्वमादृतः ।\nतदाचक्ष्वासुरेन्द्राय स च युक्तं करोतु यत् ॥७६॥',
    iast: 'tadāgacchatu śumbho\'tra niśumbho vā mahāsuraḥ |\nmāṃ jitvā kiṃ cireṇātra pāṇiṃ gṛhṇātu me laghu ||70||\ndūta uvāca |\navaliptāsi maivaṃ tvaṃ devi brūhi mamāgrataḥ |\ntrailokye kaḥ pumastiṣṭhedagre śumbhaniśumbhayoḥ ||71||\nanyeṣāmapi daityānāṃ sarve devā na vai yudhi |\ntiṣṭhanti sammukhe devi kiṃ punaḥ strī tvamekikā ||72||\nindrādyāḥ sakalā devāstasthuryeṣāṃ na saṃyuge |\nśumbhādīnāṃ kathaṃ teṣāṃ strī prayāsyasi sammukham ||73||\nsā tvaṃ gaccha mayaivoktā pārśva śumbhaniśumbhayoḥ |\nkeśākarṣaṇanirdhūtagauravā mā gamiṣyasi ||74||\nevametadbalī śumbho niśumbhaścātivīryavān |\nkiṃ karomi pratijñā me yadanālocitā purā ||75||\nsa tvaṃ gaccha mayaivoktaṃ yadetatsarvamādṛtaḥ |\ntadācakṣvāsurendrāya sa ca yuktaṃ karotu yat ||76||',
    conceptIds: ['shumbha-nishumbha', 'sadhana-samara'],
    translation: '“So let Śumbha come here, or the great demon Niśumbha; having conquered Me, why delay here — let him swiftly take My hand.” The envoy said: “Thou art conceited — speak not so before me, Goddess! What man in the triple world could stand before Śumbha-Niśumbha? Before other demons too the gods never stand face to face in battle — how much less thou, a lone woman! Before Śumbha and his kin, before whom even all the gods with Indra stood not in battle — how wilt thou, a woman, go before them? Go, as bidden by me, to Śumbha-Niśumbha’s side — lest thou go shorn of honour, dragged by the hair.” “True — mighty is Śumbha, exceeding-valiant Niśumbha. What can I do? My vow was made of old without reflection. Go thou; respectfully report all this said by me to the demon-lord — and let him do what is right.”',
    commentary: `**Sādhana-Samara Commentary (open challenge; unruffled calm):**
1. **Pāṇi-grahaṇa double edge**: “let him take My hand” — Guptavatī hears the hidden blade: pāṇiṃ gṛhṇātu = “let him receive My palm-slap” (maddhasta-capeṭā)! Laghu (swiftly, at once): no delay — “kālaḥ pibati tadrasam” (time drinks the flavour of delayed deeds). The challenge is total and immediate; there is no “later” in sādhanā. Devī’s maids (sakhīs) inwardly laugh: the “husband” can only be Mahādeva Himself.
2. **Bullying unmasked**: avaliptāsi (conceited!) — projection; gendered scorn (“lone woman”); status-threat (all gods fled); hair-dragging menace (keśākarṣaṇa — the exact humiliation Draupadī suffered; ego threatens the deepest shame). For beginners: watch temptation turn bully the moment bargaining fails — the same voice that flattered (“tremulous-glanced”) now sneers (“conceited”). Same Sugrīva, same service.
3. **“Kiṃ karomi” — helplessness as strength**: Her reply echoes Samādhi’s cry (dm-1-16, ed23/26: kiṃ karomi na badhnāti…): apparent helplessness before the vow. But here helplessness is armour — bound by truthfulness (satya), She cannot be moved by threats OR bribes. “Gaccha… ācakṣva” (go, report): dismissal with full dignity; “sa ca yuktaṃ karotu” (let him do what is right): the outcome committed to dharma. Battle now inevitable — Dhūmralocana marches (Ch6).`,
    keyPoints: [
      '**Palm-slap in the Vow**: “Take My hand” hides “take My slap” — challenge total and immediate.',
      '**Flattery Turns Bully**: Same voice that coaxed now threatens hair-dragging — recognise the turn.',
      '**Helplessness as Armour**: Bound by truthfulness, She cannot be moved by bribe or threat.'
    ]
