    devanagari: 'न चास्या वेदनां चक्रे गदापातोऽल्पिकामपि ।\nतस्याहतस्य देहात्तु बहु सुस्राव शोणितम् ॥५७॥\nयतस्ततस्तद्वक्त्रेण चामुण्डा सम्प्रतीच्छति ।\nमुखे समुद्गता येऽस्या रक्तपातान्महासुराः ॥५८॥\nतांश्चखादाथ चामुण्डा पपौ तस्य च शोणितम् ।\nदेवी शूलेन वज्रेण बाणैरसिभि ऋष्टिभिः ॥५९॥\nजघान रक्तबीजं तं चामुण्डापीतशोणितम् ।\nस पपात महीपृष्ठे शस्त्रसङ्घसमाहतः ॥६०॥\nनीरक्तश्च महीपाल रक्तबीजो महासुरः ।\nततस्ते हर्षमतुलमवापुस्त्रिदशा नृप ॥६१॥\nहते मातृगणस्तस्मिन्ननर्तासृङ्मदोद्धतः ॥६२॥',
    iast: 'na cāsyā vedanāṃ cakre gadāpāto\'lpikāmapi |\ntasyāhatasya dehāttu bahu susrāva śoṇitam ||57||\nyatastatastadvaktreṇa cāmuṇḍā sampratīcchati |\nmukhe samudgatā ye\'syā raktapātānmahāsurāḥ ||58||\ntāṃścakhādātha cāmuṇḍā papau tasya ca śoṇitam |\ndevī śūlena vajreṇa bāṇairasibhi ṛṣṭibhiḥ ||59||\njaghāna raktabījaṃ taṃ cāmuṇḍāpītaśoṇitam |\nsa papāta mahīpṛṣṭhe śastrasaṅghasamāhataḥ ||60||\nnīraktaśca mahīpāla raktabījo mahāsuraḥ |\ntataste harṣamatulamavāpustridaśā nṛpa ||61||\nhate mātṛgaṇastasminnanartāsṛṅmadoddhataḥ ||62||',
    conceptIds: ['raktabija', 'kali-chamunda', 'sadhana-samara'],
    translation: 'And no pain at all did the mace-blow cause Her, not even slight; from his much-struck body much blood flowed. Wherever, with that mouth, Cāmuṇḍā catches it — and the demons arisen in the mouth from blood-fall, those too Cāmuṇḍā devoured, and drank his blood. Then Devī slew blood-emptied Raktabīja with spear, bolt, arrows, swords and ṛṣṭis. He fell on the earth’s back, struck by weapon-masses. Blood-emptied, O king, was the great demon Raktabīja; then the gods attained matchless joy, O king. When he was slain, the Mothers danced, arrogant with blood-wine.',
    commentary: `**Sādhana-Samara Commentary (unfelt blows; blood-wine dance):**
1. **“No pain at all”**: gadāpātaḥ — the dying ego’s last mace-blows cause Her “not even slight” pain (alpikām api). Established awareness cannot be hurt by what it is dissolving; only the identified suffer blows. For beginners: when old habits lash out during withdrawal, their unfelt-ness is the sign of disidentification — note it, rejoice, do not re-engage.
2. **Method executed perfectly**: wherever (yatas-tatas) — no gap; with that mouth (tadvaktreṇa) — the spread Void; mouth-born demons devoured too (even those arisen INSIDE the mouth are eaten: witnessing catches even subtle secondary thoughts); Cāmuṇḍā drinks (papau) while Devī strikes (jaghāna) — catcher and striker in rhythm. Blood-emptied (nīrakta, Candraprabhā: rakta-hīna), weapon-mass-struck, he falls.
3. **Asṛṅ-mada dance**: the Mothers dance “arrogant with blood-wine” (Damasoddhara, Caturdharī) — transmuted desire becomes ecstasy-fuel; battle ends in festivity, as ever (cf. dm-3-39, dm-7-19). Here ends Chapter 8 (Raktabīja-vadha); Niśumbha steps forth fresh (Ch9) — for the field cleared of clones reveals the brother-duel.`,
