    devanagari: 'हंसयुक्तविमानस्थे ब्रह्माणीरूपधारिणि ।\nकौशाम्भः क्षरिके देवि नारायणि नमोऽस्तु ते ॥१२॥\nत्रिशूलचन्द्राहिधरे महावृषभवाहिनि ।\nमाहेश्वरीस्वरूपेण नारायणि नमोऽस्तु ते ॥१३॥\nमयूरकुक्कुटवृते महाशक्तिधरेऽनघे ।\nकौमारीरूपसंस्थाने नारायणि नमोऽस्तु ते ॥१४॥\nशङ्खचक्रगदाशार्ङ्गगृहीतपरमायुधे ।\nप्रसीद वैष्णवीरूपे नारायणि नमोऽस्तु ते ॥१५॥\nगृहीतोग्रमहाचक्रे दंष्ट्रोधृतवसुन्धरे ।\nवराहरूपिणि शिवे नारायणि नमोऽस्तु ते ॥१६॥\nनृसिंहरूपेणोग्रेण हन्तुं दैत्यान्कृतोद्यमे ।\nत्रैलोक्यत्राणसहिते नारायणि नमोऽस्तु ते ॥१७॥\nकिरीटिनि महावज्रे सहस्रनयनोज्ज्वले ।\nवृत्रप्राणहरे चैन्द्रि नारायणि नमोऽस्तु ते ॥१८॥\nशिवदूतीस्वरूपेण हतदैत्यमहाबले ।\nघोररूपे महारावे नारायणि नमोऽस्तु ते ॥१९॥\nदंष्ट्राकरालवदने शिरोमालाविभूषणे ।\nचामुण्डे मुण्डमथने नारायणि नमोऽस्तु ते ॥२०॥\nलक्ष्मि लज्जे महाविद्ये श्रद्धे पुष्टे स्वधे ध्रुवे ।\nमहारात्रि महामाये नारायणि नमोऽस्तु ते ॥२१॥\nमेधे सरस्वति वरे भूति बाभ्रवि तामसि ।\nनियते त्वं प्रसीदेशे नारायणि नमोऽस्तु ते ॥२२॥',
    iast: 'haṃsayuktavimānasthe brahmāṇīrūpadhāriṇi |\nkauśāmbhaḥ kṣarike devi nārāyaṇi namo\'stu te ||12||\ntriśūlacandrāhidhare mahāvṛṣabhavāhini |\nmāheśvarīsvarūpeṇa nārāyaṇi namo\'stu te ||13||\nmayūrakukkuṭavṛte mahāśaktidhare\'naghe |\nkaumārīrūpasaṃsthāne nārāyaṇi namo\'stu te ||14||\nśaṅkhacakragadāśārṅgagṛhītaparamāyudhe |\nprasīda vaiṣṇavīrūpe nārāyaṇi namo\'stu te ||15||\ngṛhītogramahācakre daṃṣṭrodhṛtavasundhare |\nvarāharūpiṇi śive nārāyaṇi namo\'stu te ||16||\nnṛsiṃharūpeṇogreṇa hantuṃ daityānkṛtodyame |\ntrailokyatrāṇasahite nārāyaṇi namo\'stu te ||17||\nkirīṭini mahāvajre sahasranayanojjvale |\nvṛtraprāṇahare caindri nārāyaṇi namo\'stu te ||18||\nśivadūtīsvarūpeṇa hatadaityamahābale |\nghorarūpe mahārāve nārāyaṇi namo\'stu te ||19||\ndaṃṣṭrākarālavadane śiromālāvibhūṣaṇe |\ncāmuṇḍe muṇḍamathane nārāyaṇi namo\'stu te ||20||\nlakṣmi lajje mahāvidye śraddhe puṣṭe svadhe dhruve |\nmahārātri mahāmāye nārāyaṇi namo\'stu te ||21||\nmedhe sarasvati vare bhūti bābhravi tāmasi |\nniyate tvaṃ prasīdeśe nārāyaṇi namo\'stu te ||22||',
    conceptIds: ['narayani-stuti', 'matrikas', 'cit-shakti'],
    translation: '“O Thou throned on the swan-car, wearing Brahmāṇī’s form, O pourer of kuśa-blessed water — salutation to Thee, Nārāyaṇī! O trident-moon-serpent bearer, greatly bull-borne, in Māheśvarī form — salutation! O peacock-cock-attended, great-power-bearing, sinless, abiding in Kaumārī form — salutation! O supreme-weapon-wielding conch-discus-mace-bow — be gracious in Vaiṣṇavī form — salutation! O fierce-great-discus-wielding, earth uplifting with tusk, in boar-form, gracious — salutation! O striving with fierce Nṛsiṃha-form to slay demons, with triple-world rescue — salutation! O diademed, great-thunderbolted, thousand-eyed-radiant, Vṛtra’s-life-stealing Aindrī — salutation! O Śivadūtī-formed, slayer of the demon host, dread-formed, great-roaring — salutation! O fanged-dread-faced, head-garland-adorned Cāmuṇḍā, churner of Muṇḍa — salutation! O Lakṣmī, Lajjā, Mahāvidyā, Śraddhā, Puṣṭi, Svadhā, Dhruvā, Mahārātri, Mahāmāyā — salutation! O Medhā, Sarasvatī, Varā, Bhūti, Bābhravī, Tāmasī, Niyatā — be gracious, O Īśe — salutation!”',
    commentary: `**Sādhana-Samara Commentary (battle-forms become praise-forms):**
1. **Same Mothers, new light**: Brāhmī (kuśa-water pourer — Guptavatī/Caturdharī: sanctified sprinkling), Māheśvarī, Kaumārī, Vaiṣṇavī (“prasīda” — be gracious IN that form: even praise asks!), Vārāhī, Nārasiṃhī, Aindrī (mahāvajra — thunderbolt emended), Śivadūtī, Cāmuṇḍā — the Ch8 battle-line returns as litany. Assimilation complete: yesterday’s weapons are today’s names. For beginners: re-meet your fiercest practices as beloved forms.
2. **Lakṣmī-quartet in -e vocatives**: Lakṣmī, Lajjā, Mahāvidyā, Śraddhā, Puṣṭi, Svadhā, Dhruvā, Mahārātri, Mahāmāyā — grace’s roll-call, each a Vedic -e endearment. Then Medhā-Sarasvatī-Varā-Bhūti (wisdom, flow, boon, being) — the gentle close of the fierce catalogue. Note the movement: war-goddesses → grace-goddesses → wisdom-goddesses.
3. **Nārāyaṇī repeated**: every verse lands on the same refrain — Nārāyaṇa’s (indwelling Self’s) active counterpart. Repetition is the method: one Name, many faces, single surrender. Protection-prayers follow (dm-11-23).`,
